  This module declares the permissions it actually uses, so that any consumer of
  :core:network inherits them through manifest merging rather than having to know.
  Both are also declared in :app; the merger de-duplicates them.

  AC-NFR-04 caps the app at exactly these two. Adding a third here would silently widen
  the app's permission set, so treat this file as part of that budget.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />

</manifest>
